  "body": "Direct-PR: daily docs-only ledger fold by the docs steward (AGENTS.md §8, the ledger #620); a ledger PR needs no adversarial review and merges on green CI.\n\nListed PRs: #638 #686 #690.\n\nReproduce on the base: `python3 tooling/docs/ledger.py fold --apply --prs 638 686 690 && git diff --exit-code <head>` shows no difference (checked: empty diff).\n\nWhat changed: `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` and `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md` only (rows, H.1 lists and Counts regenerated by the script). Folded 3, skipped 0.\n\nLeft for a human (not applied by this PR):\n- 21 `BY HAND CONFLICT` cells where #690 and #686 set the same GAP cell differently: the earlier merge (#686) keeps its text, #690's wording is not applied (GAP-093, 099, 152, 186, 210, 215, 217, 219). The decision is the operator's.\n- `ledger-note` blocks of #686 and #690 (legend wording, header Source bullet, \"Not in these rows\", Convergence notes 10, H.1 bullet of 216, UXD-01 and UXD-25 \"Recorded in\"): they go in a reviewed PR on branch `docs/ledger-notes-<date>`, not here.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEBkjmFApUaMrewUvD)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated the legacy changelog with details on opening member menus, blacklist and whitelist actions, read conversation title color, and topic page cache duration and size limits.\n  * Expanded the migration comparison with revised details and classifications for favourites, video embeds, archived drafts, polls, reply modes, settings, cache behavior, device layouts, and multiple windows. Updated the related counts and convergence lists.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
