   "body": "<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/696?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\" alt=\"Explain Change →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> ## Review failed\n> \n> The pull request is closed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Walkthrough</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\nThe changelog adds and reinserts feature entries. The migration gap report revises legacy-versus-Swift comparisons, device-layout details, classifications, and counts.\n\n**Changes: Legacy documentation updates**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Changelog feature entries** <br> `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md`|Adds entries for opening a member menu, list settings and actions, the read-conversation title color, and topic-page cache limits. Entries `#640` and `#651` are reinserted without observable changes.|\n|**Legacy behavior comparisons** <br> `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`|Updates comparisons for topic reading, video embeds, avatars, archived drafts, poll creation, reply controls, and private-message actions.|\n|**Settings and cache comparisons** <br> `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`|Adds legacy settings and cache details, including the legacy 7-day/50 MB cache limits and SwiftHFR’s 1-day/20 MB limits.|\n|**Device layout comparisons** <br> `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`|Adds legacy details for device layouts, fold handoff, and multi-window support.|\n|**Gap counts and classifications** <br> `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`|Updates gap totals and H.1 classification lists and counts.|\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Estimated code review effort:** 2 (Simple) | ~10 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"609c236db088433e839c162a3d053ae9ad5c2f9e\" -->\n**Change:** Other\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n**Possibly related issues**\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#379` — The PR changes H.1 classifications for archived drafts and poll creation, which are among the lots discussed in this issue.\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#655` — The PR adds later legacy commit references to the gap report, matching this issue’s request to map legacy commits.\n\n**Suggested labels:** `direct-pr`\n\n**Suggested reviewers:** `ezzz`\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-low-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Low</strong> · up to <code>609c2</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **🔵 Low** · up to `609c2`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"609c236db088433e839c162a3d053ae9ad5c2f9e\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"609c236db088433e839c162a3d053ae9ad5c2f9e\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThis docs-only change updates the legacy-versus-Swift gap report. One convergence-notes list still places four M4 lots in M5, which could mislead planning until the planned ledger-notes PR fixes it. No runtime or user-facing behavior is affected.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\"} --> <strong title=\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\n<!-- operational_warnings_start -->\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: all tool run failures by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Some tools did not complete. Review the errors below.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/wrench-dark.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/wrench.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> LanguageTool</strong></summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary><strong>docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md</strong></summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> LanguageTool could not check every text chunk; analysis is incomplete\n> \n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: all tool run failures by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- operational_warnings_end -->",
